From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Belousov <michael.belousov98@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:12:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] web: send only the GL state a draw changes

Every GL call is a trip to the GPU process in some browsers (Firefox), and each draw
sent the whole state: program, buffers, layout, texture, matrix, scissor, some 25
calls where 3 or 4 change. The program, buffers and sampler are now bound once, and
cached setters (bindTex, bindFb, setScissor, setViewport, setUseTex, setMatrix,
setLayout) send the rest only when it differs.

Each render target gets a framebuffer of its own, attached once, instead of the one
shared framebuffer re-attached on every switch, which made the driver check it again
each time. The canvas is resized only when its size changed: setting width or height,
even to the same value, makes a new drawing buffer.
